  "card": "Rewrites the torcontrol fuzz target to route traffic through a mocked DynSock connection to a simulated Tor daemon rather than directly invoking TorController callbacks. The simulated Tor answers commands with valid wire replies for PROTOCOLINFO, SAFECOOKIE challenges, GETINFO, and ADD_ONION, while verifying that the controller only uses offered auth methods, uses fresh nonces, and advertises the correct onion service. It also fixes a bug in the DynSock::Wait test utility that caused the socket to destroy itself. Author reports line coverage on src/torcontrol.cpp increases from 52% to 81%.",
